conspiracy. As the evidence in support of a charge of conspiracy is often
circumstantial, the actual facts of the conspiracy may be inferred from
the collateral circumstances of the case. A charge of conspiracy can often
be proved only by an inference of the subsequent conduct of the parties
in committing some overt acts, which tend so obviously towards the
alleged unlawful results as to suggest that they must have arisen from
an agreement to bring them about.”
In Kehar Singh vs State (Delhi Admin) AIR1988 SC1883 (Indira Gandhi
