his torch, as the incident occurred around 8.00 p.m. The duration of the witness’s
observation would have been very brief, as the identification was made while both
parties were in motion. The distance from which PW3 made this observation was
approximately 50 feet. The witness clearly stated that he directed the torchlight
and identified the appellant. He testified as follows:
