17. Also, the testimony provided by PW01 asserting that the first accused
appellant physically restrained him at the scene of the initial
confrontation is demonstrably contradicted by his earlier deposition
given during the non-summary inquiry conducted at the Magistrates
Court in Kalutara. In those proceedings, PW01 has explicitly stated that
the fifth accused as named in the indictment was the individual who held
him. This material contradiction has been formally marked and identified
as exhibit 1වි1.
18. Accordingly, the testimony of PW01 concerning the appellants
identification has been irreconcilable yet no explanation has been offered
for the resulting discrepancies. Consequently, the disputed judgment
does not demonstrate an engagement with these critical inconsistencies.
