38. It must be emphasized that the subjective state of mind of an accused at the time of
inflicting a fatal injury is not ordinarily capable of direct proof and can ordinarily
only be inferred from all the circumstances leading up to and surrounding the act.
39. In the present case, the evidence shows that the appellant had no intention of
