45. As noted earlier, the cut injuries sustained by the appellant on his fingers, although
not conclusively established as having been caused during the struggle for the knife,
were corroborated by the evidence of the doctor who testified for the defence. The
doctor stated that such injuries could have been inflicted while the appellant was
