had reported to work at a garage. Nevertheless, she stated that after the incident she went
to Hemasiri’s house, accompanied by her children, to see whether Hemasiri was there so
that he could accompany them to the police.
13. When questioned by the defence counsel as to why she went to Hemasiri’s house if she
knew he was not at home that day, she failed to provide an answer. At page 137, the
inconsistent nature of her evidence is further apparent, as PW1 stated that Hemasiri was not
on good terms with her and never visited her, yet she also claimed that when they were in
need of money, he used to come and provide financial assistance. She testified as follows:
